{"title":"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4db12271a376d5435b4c452eabf2a51df029d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^\\circ$\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /> rise in temperature, the volume of a certain gas expands by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cubic centimeters.  If the volume of the gas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cubic centimeters when the temperature is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1fd38aa0002fcd875600f3b2975cd81561ebafd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, what was the volume of the gas in cubic centimeters when the temperature was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9498d610c387e904044dd016ade3bc445cb5d100.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897d873d7cf9a7874290fd918e469ed79a3a0b16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 15 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 16 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The temperature increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6ccbdcc4a17fd21bcfdc9286a9c6a01e929a2bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, so it increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faff50ed7c4ec1b9eafa339eb386d2d5942799e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> four times.  Since each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faff50ed7c4ec1b9eafa339eb386d2d5942799e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> increase caused the volume of the gas to expand by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cubic centimeters, the gas expanded by a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c0637a8a49dd1bc93c7ea16d0b1d22c26f9714e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> cubic centimeters.  Therefore, the original volume of the gas was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e850d05c37124154ff20a5e8af97aab4dc269b64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 - 16 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" /> cubic centimeters.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the temperature in degrees and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the volume of the gas.  Since a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faff50ed7c4ec1b9eafa339eb386d2d5942799e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> increase in the temperature causes a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cubic centimeter expansion, the relationship between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is linear and has slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33bd495b7492f95385da7afb197cd34638cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.  Using point-slope form with the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b100225ba47690422050fb01322700b43e70b96b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(32, 24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, the equation of this relationship is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/7/14733ab5143fc1f3892d290be6ba504474822528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{4}{3}(x-32) + 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" />.  Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/501e01049152d68121e7508cfdb86e345cc25ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 20$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99f33fa2fd2a12048f59b6ff93bcba4456cb7c3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"91\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME\" title=\"1991 AJHSME\">1991 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1991\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl